{#- Générateur du corpus documentaire synthétique + questions annotées (famille RAG). -#}
"""Synthetic corpus generator of the retrieval-augmented generation family.

{{ wrap(spec.data.description, 98) }}

The generator is *not* a random text generator: it plants **facts** (a sentence carrying a
value) into documents, then writes the questions from those facts. That is what makes the
evaluation meaningful:

* each question knows which document answers it, and which sentence contains the answer, so
  recall@k and citation precision measure something real;
* some questions are paraphrases that share almost no word with the source sentence, which is
  where a lexical retriever must fail and a good embedding must win;
* some questions are answered by **two** documents (a procedure and its exception), which
  punishes any system that stops at the first plausible passage;
* a share of the questions has **no answer** in the corpus (``hors_corpus``): the only correct
  behaviour is to abstain, and the schema refuses to let such a question carry a fake gold span.

Everything is seeded: two calls with the same configuration produce byte-identical frames.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

